{"seq":1,"ts":"2026-11-07T07:23:13.215Z","type":"exp.start","exp":"E-CMP-INVEST-02","attempt":1,"title":"Investing together, each backer funding their own amount: per-member charges against equal shares, same backers, same run","tier":"testnet","hypothesis":"Predictions written first in docs/lab/USECASE_PLAN.md. Four backers put in 0.01, 0.02, 0.03 and 0.04 NEAR through the same room with a common 0.05 deposit. (1) With the pooled program and settle_batch_charged each backer's remainder at exit is exactly their deposit less their own amount (0.04, 0.03, 0.02, 0.01). (2) But the charges are arguments of the public settlement transaction, so an observer reading only that transaction recovers all four contributions. (3) With an ordinary equal-share settlement the same observer recovers none, and each backer bears 0.025 whatever they put in. (4) Before either round settles the escrows are all equal and say nothing. So for pooled investing, hiding the amounts and funding each backer fairly are not both available on this contract. Fails if the observer cannot recover the contributions from the charged settlement, if a remainder differs from deposit less contribution, or if the equal-share round leaks any amount.","limits":["One operator controls every account; the room is a local HostedRoost with a simulated attestation provider.","The observer reads the settlement transaction's public arguments through an archival RPC, which is what an explorer shows. It does not model an attacker who also sees the room.","Hiding the charges (the room signing per-member receipts that members claim against, or zero-knowledge proofs) is not built and not tested; it is named in the plan as a design option.","Amounts are tiny testnet NEAR. Bids are not authenticated to an account (GAP-023)."],"requires":["near-key","network"],"chain_prev":"365cf145dd0bd4b4b8329d8c79789e526d3899bad9a57071f6c0adbf7c38a75d","chain_hash":"b8240af59808733a49fe917e48a81b8d03ecb0042b40bf9f4df48737de75f117"}
